{"content":[{"c":["EUTYCHUS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common slave name, mentioned only in ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.20.9","r":"Acts.20.9","rawR":"Acts.20.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.20.9","value":"Acts.20.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 20:9"},". It was Eutychus’s misfortune to become sleepy while sitting on a windowsill listening to the apostle Paul preach at Troas. He sank into a deep sleep and fell from the ledge, which was in the third loft. The apostle Paul revived him from the dead (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.20.7-12","r":"Acts.20.7-12","rawR":"Acts.20.7-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.20.7-12","value":"Acts.20.7-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"7-12"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eutychus","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 20:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.20.9","rawQueryValue":"Acts.20.9","sourceRefExact":"Acts.20.9"},{"anchorText":"7-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.20.7-12","rawQueryValue":"Acts.20.7-12","sourceRefExact":"Acts.20.7-12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a08bacd0310d92fdccbbcc63a37b760f97557543e42f566f31c928d5f372beff","sourceItemName":"Eutychus","sourceItemOrder":279,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Eutychus","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Eutychus","title":"Eutychus","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}